    "title": "Carbamazepine contraindicated with DTG",
    "message": "Guidelines list carbamazepine as a contraindication for DTG, and state it decreases DTG levels by 30–70%. Carbamazepine was started 2 weeks ago, coinciding with viral load rising from <50 to 1,240 copies/mL despite reported good adherence. This interaction is the likely cause of virological failure. The guideline recommends using valproic acid instead of carbamazepine for patients on DTG.",
    "issue_type": "drug_interaction",
    "severity": "critical",
    "recommended_action": "Replace carbamazepine with valproic acid or another non-interacting antiepileptic. If carbamazepine is unavoidable, consider switching ART regimen per specialist advice.",
